footnote: "Includes data from the following sources: 2021 OECD Survey on Drivers of Trust in Public Institutions; 2022 OECD Survey on Drivers of Trust in Public Institutions, https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/drivers-of-trust-in-public-institutions-in-brazilfb0e1896-en/full-report.html; 2023 OECD Survey on Drivers of Trust in Public Institutions; Encuesta Nacional de Calidad e Impacto Gubernamental (ENCIG); Encuesta Nacional de Calidad e Impacto Gubernamental (ENCIG) 2021. Seccion V. Evaluacion de los servicios publicos bajo demanda; Enquete Module et Permanente Aupres des Menages (EMOP); Questionnaire , Passage 3, EMOP Section SHaSA2, module harmonise sur la paix et la Securite (18 ans et plus); Enquete nationale sur la perception de la population tunisienne en matiere de securite, de libertes et de gouvernance locale; Gallup World Poll; Governance, Public Safety, and Justice Survey (GPSJS) 2019/2020; Governance, Public Safety, and Justice Survey (GPSJS) 2022/23; OECD Survey on Drivers of Trust in Public Institutions, 2021; SOCIAL SURVEY 2015; Sample household living standards survey; Satisfaction Index of Public Administrative Services; Satisfaction Survey for the Citizens Service Center (2020); Satisfaction Survey for the Citizens Service Center (2023); Satisfaction survey on public services; Satisfaction survey on public services, 2022; Social-Economic Conditions Survey, 2020-Main Findings Section 10: Mobility and Access to Basic Services; Survey of Lithuanian resident's opinions on state and municipal institutions and agencies anr their provided services; Survey of people's satisfaction with the services of government agencies; The Citizen survey, i.e., Innbyggerunderskelsen, carried out by The Norwegian Agency for Public and Financial Management (DF). The general topic of the survey is to measure citizen attitudes and trust in the public sector; The Gambia 2020-21 SDGs Monitoring Survey; The citizen survey. The responsible government agency is the Norwegian Agency for Public and Financial Management (DF)"

